{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And to the people you shall say: Sanctify yourselves for tomorrow.</b> Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote that the reason it said 'and to the people you shall say: Sanctify yourselves for tomorrow' and did not inform them, saying 'I am giving them meat tomorrow' — in the manner said of the other miracles (Exodus 16:4): ״הנני ממטיר לכם״, (Exodus 17:6): ״הנני עומד לפניך שם על הצור״ — Moses understood that it was not the will of the Holy One, blessed be He, that the giving of the meat should come about by way of miracle from Him, blessed be He, but rather by way of nature."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Source cites (שמות ט״ז:ד׳) for the first quotation, which is Exodus 16:4; the second quotation is from Exodus 17:6 but bears no explicit citation in the source — normalized for clarity."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:31:21.793731327Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}